Z||000010||loafer87gt||08-02-2000||05:06 PM||||I find it works good for removing boot scuff marks on the door sills of my GT. Spray on , and wipe off, whoila!||||reg||1
Z||000011||SpeedPhreak||08-02-2000||07:46 PM||||stops squeeks. cleans motorcycle chains (even o-ring chains) & is also great for cleaning brake dust & chain wax off of motorcycle rims (although brake cleaner works a tad bit better).  helps get rubber grommets into & out of place.<P>i second the spraying of fishing lures.||||reg||1
Z||000012||olympic||08-02-2000||08:47 PM||||   It makes a nice flame thrower.  Ether is bettrer though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||stsmithgt||08-03-2000||11:18 AM||||Speaking of fire.  It burns slow enough, especially when you let it soak in to be used to start a campfire or at least start your kindling with it.  OK I like playing with fire. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||deceler8||08-04-2000||04:33 PM||||Keeps omelettes from sticking to my fry pan and gives a nice vanilla scent to warm bread (oh sorry, that's off the Martha Stewart "Using WD40" section of her webpage...<P>WD40 really is about the one tool I'll never be without. ||||reg||1
